 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Great plan. For a eight year old, a day at the museum or theater is about the right age. That's the shrimp tank show at the museum. They flip the shrimp over so you see the other side. Most museums and theaters offer cheap kid tickets, often free with ticket for an adult. Try something sweet at the snack shop, or keep snacks in your bag. Give his attention to the show, and the snacks will keep him content. That way he can choose whether he wants to see the shrimp or the big robot, and the snacks will keep him happy.",
